  "approach": "Teach how to say where people are from (ser de + country, ser + nationality), the three patterns of nationality words, and that nationalities are lowercase while countries are capitalized.",
  "coverage": [
    "¿De dónde eres? Soy de Estados Unidos. Soy estadounidense.",
    "Nationalities are lowercase: mexicano, colombiana. Countries are capitalized: México, Colombia",
    "Pattern 1, -o / -a: mexicano, mexicana; colombiano, colombiana",
    "Pattern 2, one form in -e: estadounidense, canadiense, costarricense, nicaragüense",
    "Pattern 3, consonant + a: español, española; inglés, inglesa; alemán, alemana",
    "Estadounidense is the clearest word for someone from the US; americano can mean anyone from the Americas"
  ],
